directive:
Owner directive 2026-10-07: the team's model routing goes through the single entrypoint node ~/.agents/skills/cliproxy-router/cliproxy.mjs, and VOMEGA gets a PROJECT overlay (skill doc: <repo>/.zcode/cliproxy-router.json replaces the named global profiles; it cannot add new profile names, and cannot override a hard drop). Create .zcode/cliproxy-router.json with EXACTLY this content (it is a full replacement of the five profiles, so the avoid lists restate the global drops):

{
  "schema": "cliproxy-router-policy.v1",
  "profiles": {
    "fast": {
      "description": "VOMEGA short work: sweeps, pm:check, cheap probes. Cheap live models only.",
      "prefer_patterns": [
        "haiku",
        "flash",
        "build-fast"
      ],
      "avoid_patterns": [
        "imagine",
        "video",
        "mini",
        "opus-5"
      ]
    },
    "build": {
      "description": "DEV implementation: D1 red->green against exact gates. Instruction-following families first.",
      "prefer_patterns": [
        "gpt-",
        "opus",
        "sonnet"
      ],
      "avoid_patterns": [
        "imagine",
        "video",
        "mini"
      ]
    },
    "reason": {
      "description": "COUNCIL chair and hard gate-law debugging. Strongest live reasoner; COUNCIL passes an explicit id when it needs a named family.",
      "prefer_patterns": [
        "opus",
        "sol"
      ],
      "avoid_patterns": [
        "imagine",
        "video",
        "mini",
        "fast"
      ]
    },
    "review": {
      "description": "Independent review. Defaults to a family different from a GPT-based implementer; COUNCIL passes an explicit id when it needs a named family.",
      "prefer_patterns": [
        "opus",
        "sonnet"
      ],
      "avoid_patterns": [
        "imagine",
        "video"
      ]
    },
    "long-context": {
      "description": "Reading the D1 codebase and long files.",
      "prefer_patterns": [
        "opus",
        "gpt-6",
        "sol"
      ],
      "avoid_patterns": [
        "imagine",
        "video",
        "mini"
      ]
    }
  }
}

Then verify and report, per profile, the output of: node ~/.agents/skills/cliproxy-router/cliproxy.mjs route <profile> --project C:/0-BlackBoxProject-0/VOMEGA for profile in fast build reason review long-context. Expected properties to state explicitly: (a) 'policy' is 'project' for all five; (b) review selects a claude-* id (opus/sonnet), which is the point: a different family from a GPT-based implementer; (c) no selected id contains imagine/video/mini/fast; (d) cooled models never appear in candidates. Do NOT edit ~/.zcode/cliproxy-router/policy.json, config.yaml, auth files or provider_config.json. Do not print any key. Commit ONLY .zcode/cliproxy-router.json. Also add two lines to .project/dev-loop/PROVIDER-AVAILABILITY.md (your file): that claude-*/gpt-*/grok-*/codex-* ids are CPA-routed and their live selection is decided by the entrypoint above, while port 6446 (new-provider, opencode-acct-2..5) and openrouter are NOT CPA and stay outside it; and that the hand-maintained dark list is a RECORD, not the decision input (the router excludes cooled/unroutable models itself). Reply DONE with the five route outputs, the commit hashes, and any profile whose selection you would change.
